 Terms of a Sequence Using Function Notation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ec440bfe-ea82-57e4-97da-c797c45e181e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186564348}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ec440bfe-ea82-57e4-97da-c797c45e181e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186564348} :answer-field/id #uuid "92fed66e-500f-5762-be56-7e7c4552f0c6" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186564422} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5012a895-a225-58c1-9810-e7dffea25a49" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "35" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186564097}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5012a895-a225-58c1-9810-e7dffea25a49" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "35" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186564097} :answer-field/id #uuid "cde7e62d-c2d6-5dd4-8154-82d02af8a287" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186564441}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "4c253992-f8f6-54f1-85fd-c768c36b2399" :question/math-academy-id "q-223474" :question/problem "A sequence is defined as $f(n)={n}^{2}-1$ for $n\\ge 1.$ What are the $3$rd and $6$th terms of the sequence?\n\nThe $3$rd term is\n{{field-1}}\nand the $6$th term is\n{{field-2}}." :question/worked-solution "Using the definition of the sequence, we find the $3$rd and $6$th terms corresponding to $n=3$ and $n=6,$ respectively:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(3) & ={3}^{2}-1=8 \\\\ f(6) & ={6}^{2}-1=35\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the $3$rd term is $8$ and the $6$th term is $35.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186564524 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186138455 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "d85ef216-095d-589d-8d1d-5a1543d576a3" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying the Terms of a Sequence Given as a List"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a775068e-f991-59be-b61c-3d9f355a74b9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "14" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186564224}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a775068e-f991-59be-b61c-3d9f355a74b9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "14" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186564224} :answer-field/id #uuid "dad9a537-c8c8-5a4d-92d7-f01642118b81" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186564448} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b245a09b-ec25-541f-85cc-5f78e8d65ee1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "42" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186564247}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b245a09b-ec25-541f-85cc-5f78e8d65ee1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "42" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186564247} :answer-field/id #uuid "ee083db5-3ee1-5761-a700-038e4b0040ba" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186564455}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "d2d2cf77-d5f7-5477-9cd1-8f7ee0800051" :question/math-academy-id "q-262870" :question/problem "What are the second and last terms of the following sequence? \n\n$$\n7,\\,14,\\,21,\\,28,\\,35,\\,42\n$$\n\nThe second term is\n{{field-1}}\nand the last term is\n{{field-2}}." :question/worked-solution "For this sequence:\n\n- The first term is $7$\n\n- The second term is $14$\n\n- The third term is $21$\n\n- The fourth term is $28$\n\n- The fifth term is $35$\n\n- The sixth term is $42$\n\nTherefore, the second term is $14$ and the last term is $42.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186564465 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186138457 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "83b12b3a-2b6d-5fc4-80bb-c83415486b29" :knowledge-point/title "Computing the Terms of a Sequence Using Sequence Notation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4dcaad24-9937-5eb5-8e1b-2b214068fe9e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-88" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186564095}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4dcaad24-9937-5eb5-8e1b-2b214068fe9e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-88" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186564095} :answer-field/id #uuid "ab59f18d-be7d-5017-adf7-171d8d1ade47" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186564429}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "041652e3-e5d6-50e5-af62-e1885be6626d" :question/math-academy-id "q-263003" :question/problem "If a sequence is defined as ${a}_{n}=7-3{n}^{2}$ for $n\\ge 1,$ then the sum of the third and fifth terms is{{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "We substitute $n=3$ and $n=5$ into the definition of the sequence:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{3} & =7-3(3)^{2}=-20 \\\\ {a}_{5} & =7-3(5)^{2}=-68\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the sum of the third and fifth terms is\n\n$$\n{a}_{3}+{a}_{5}=(-20)+(-68)=-88.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186564497 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186138455 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "d85ef216-095d-589d-8d1d-5a1543d576a3" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying the Terms of a Sequence Given as a List"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "12760c89-057a-56