gin{aligned}f(n) & =3n-1 \\\\ f(5) & =3(5)-1 \\\\ f(5) & =14\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the $5$th term is $14.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186564536 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186138457 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "83b12b3a-2b6d-5fc4-80bb-c83415486b29" :knowledge-point/title "Computing the Terms of a Sequence Using Sequence Notation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "100fb983-8d65-541a-b869-4fc441d08865" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "11" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563993} {:answer/id #uuid "51e57a9c-0b53-5fd2-8134-d370f512590e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186564099} {:answer/id #uuid "522626a5-bf0b-54d0-a6e0-40e3923844ad" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "17" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186564100} {:answer/id #uuid "8ab5a3bb-590b-57a6-9513-86017a2683ad" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "23" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186564183} {:answer/id #uuid "bcba76b5-246f-56ae-8cd3-76cbae67ed37" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186564258}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "522626a5-bf0b-54d0-a6e0-40e3923844ad" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "17" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186564100} :answer-field/id #uuid "4cf5687d-1b58-5d00-a36e-60929c2459dd" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186564394}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "f29afdcb-efb1-549b-8468-0f53b64a94c5" :question/math-academy-id "q-61145" :question/problem "A sequence is defined as ${a}_{n}=3n-2$ for $n\\ge 1.$ What is the sum of the third and fourth terms?" :question/worked-solution "We substitute $n=3$ and $n=4$ into the definition of the sequence:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{3} & =3(3)-2=7 \\\\ {a}_{4} & =3(4)-2=10\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the sum of the third and fourth terms is\n\n$$\n{a}_{3}+{a}_{4}=7+10=17.\n$$"}]}
